msgstr "Takrifkan masalah MVC rawak dengan menjana graf dengan nod berwajaran rawak.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/extracted-outputs/c2ce65e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/extracted-outputs/c2ce65e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A standard optimization model for weighted graph partitioning can be formulated as follows. Split the nodes of the graph into three groups $g \\in \\{0, 1, 2\\}$, and let $n_{i,g} = 1$ if node $i$ is assigned to group $g$, and $n_{i,g} = 0$ otherwise. The goal is to minimize the total weight of edges whose endpoints are assigned to the same group, where the weight of an edge $(i,j)$ is the combined weight of its two endpoints, $\\omega_{i,j} = \\omega_i + \\omega_j$:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\textbf{Minimize}\\qquad y = \\sum_{(i,j)\\in E} \\omega_{i,j} \\sum_{g} n_{i,g}\\, n_{j,g}$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\textbf{Minimize}\\qquad y = \\sum_{(i,j)\\in E} \\omega_{i,j} \\sum_{g} n_{i,g}\\, n_{j,g}$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every node must be assigned to exactly one of the three groups. This is a Hamming-weight-1 constraint: for every node $i$, exactly one of $n_{i,0}, n_{i,1}, n_{i,2}$ must equal 1, and the rest must equal 0:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$n_{i,0} + n_{i,1} + n_{i,2} = 1 \\texttt{ for all } i \\in V$$\n"
msgstr "$$n_{i,0} + n_{i,1} + n_{i,2} = 1 \\texttt{ for all } i \\in V$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rather than encoding this requirement as a penalty term in the cost function, pass it directly to the Solver as a hard constraint using the `constraint` input.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Partially constrained problems\">\n"
"You do not need to add every variable to `constraint`. Any variable left out of the dictionary remains unconstrained, so you can mix hard-constrained groups of variables with free variables in the same problem.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Run the problem {#2-run-the-problem-1}"
msgstr "2. Jalankan masalah {#2-run-the-problem-1}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Get the result {#3-get-the-result}"
msgstr "3. Dapatkan keputusan {#3-get-the-result}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve the solution and analyze the results. The solution cost represents the total weight of edges whose endpoints ended up in the same group, so a lower cost indicates a better partitioning of the graph.\n"
msgstr ""

